Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:57:22 +0200
Subject: configure: add PAL directory options
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add build-time PAL_PLUGIN_DIR, PAL_CONFIG_DIR, and PAL_DATA_DIR
substitutions. Defaults preserve the existing upstream layout:
plugins under libdir and configuration/data files under /etc.

Assisted-By: GPT:gpt-6-astra
Forwarded: https://github.com/AudioReach/audioreach-pal/pull/92

Signed-off-by: Lukas Märdian <lukas.maerdian@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 README.md                          | 14 ++++++++++++++
 configure.ac                       | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 plugins/vui_interface/configure.ac |  8 +++++++-
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c3bd791..370637e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,6 +6,20 @@ Audioreach-PAL (AudioReach Platform Abstraction Layer) is hardware absration lay
 
 To be available soon.
 
+## Autotools installation directories
+
+`configure` accepts the following directory options:
+
+| Option | Default | Contents |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `--with-pal-plugin-dir=DIR` | `${libdir}` | PAL plugin libraries |
+| `--with-pal-config-dir=DIR` | `/etc` | `plugin_manager.xml` and `usecaseKvManager.xml` |
+| `--with-pal-data-dir=DIR` | `/etc` | Mixer paths and resource-manager XML files |
+
+These directories are also used at runtime. `DESTDIR` only stages installation;
+it is not part of the runtime paths. When building `plugins/vui_interface`
+separately, pass the same `--with-pal-plugin-dir` option to its `configure`.
+
